Tested the state-preserving reload end-to-end. Four of five scenarios pass cleanly: window scroll position restores within 2px; the drawer reopens on the same project+step with its scroll offset, typed Executive-note text, and caret/selection range all intact; the dashboard multi-select Family filter survives; and the focused element regains focus. 

One real bug reproduced (high severity): uncommitted text typed into a dropzone note input (`.dz-note-input`) is silently lost after reload — the field comes back empty. Root cause: `captureUiState()` (system/app.js:229) only snapshots inputs with a non-empty `id`, but `.dz-note-input` (line 4800) and the gate-note input (line 4751) are created without an `id`. Report written to `qa-reports/agent3.json` (`all_passed: false`).
